<title>USA: TENNIS-RESULTS AT EVERT CUP WOMEN'S TOURNAMENT.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-RESULTS AT EVERT CUP WOMEN'S TOURNAMENT.</headline>
<dateline>INDIAN WELLS, California 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from</p>
<p>the $1.25 million Evert Cup women's tennis tournament Friday</p>
<p>(prefix number denotes seedings):</p>
<p>First round:</p>
<p>12-Elena Likhovtseva (Russia) beat Katarina Studenikova</p>
<p>(Slovakia) 7-6 (7-2) 4-6 7-5</p>
<p>13-Nathalie Tauziat (France) beat Stephanie De Ville</p>
<p>(Belgium) 6-1 6-0</p>
<p>14-Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania) beat Kristina Brandi (U.S.)</p>
<p>6-4 7-5</p>
<p>15-Chanda Rubin (U.S.) beat Amy Frazier (U.S.) 6-3 4-6 7-6</p>
<p>(8-6)</p>
<p>16-Lisa Raymond (U.S.) beat Jana Kandarr (Germany) 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>Helena Sukova (Czech Republic) beat Gloria Pizzichini (Italy)</p>
<p>6-1 5-7 6-2</p>
<p>Anna Kournikova (Russia) beat Patricia Hy-Boulais (Canada)</p>
<p>1-6 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>Venus Williams (U.S.) beat Anne Miller (U.S.) 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>Asa Carlsson (Sweden) beat Barbara Schett (Austria) 6-7 (4-7)</p>
<p>6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Larisa Neiland (Latvia) beat Magdalena Grzybowska (Poland)</p>
<p>6-7 (5-7) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Alexia Dechaume-Balleret (France) beat Karin Kschwendt</p>
<p>(Austria) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Olga Barabanschikova (Belarus) beat Alexandra Stevenson</p>
<p>(U.S.) 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>Petra Begerow (Germany) beat Catalina Cristea (Romania) 6-7</p>
<p>(2-7) 6-1 6-1</p>
<p>Elena Makarova (Russia) beat Paola Suarez (Argentina) 6-4 7-6</p>
<p>(7-4)</p>
<p>Florencia Labat (Argentina) beat Kristina Triska (Sweden) 6-2</p>
<p>6-1</p>
<p>Ai Sugiyama (Japan) beat Naoka Kijimuta (Japan) 6-4 6-7 (2-7)</p>
<p>7-6 (7-1)</p>
<p>Sadrine Testud (France) beat Anne-Gaelle Sidot (France) 6-7</p>
<p>(5-7) 7-5 6-2</p>
<p>Tami Whitlinger-Jones (U.S) beat Kristie Boogert</p>
<p>(Netherlands) 5-7 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Naoka Sawamatsu (Japan) beat Marlene Weingartner (Germany)</p>
<p>5-7 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Silvia Farina (Italy) beat Nana Miyagi (Japan) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Barbara Rittner (Germany) beat Tamarine Tanasugarn (Thailand)</p>
<p>5-7 6-0 6-2</p>
</text>
